# Cloudflare Pages redirect map.
#
# This site is a static export, so there is no server to handle redirects — this
# file is the only mechanism. It is copied into the build output automatically
# because it lives in /public.
#
# Syntax:  <from>  <to>  <status>
# Rules are evaluated top to bottom. First match wins. Limit: 2,100 rules.
# Splats (/blog/*) and placeholders (/:slug) are supported.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# BEFORE LAUNCH: inventory the URLs the old site actually had, then map each one.
#
# How to get that list:
#   1. Google Search Console -> Indexing -> Pages -> "Indexed" (export the table)
#   2. Your current host's page list (GHL funnels, Wix pages, etc.)
#   3. Any link-in-bio or QR codes already printed or posted on LinkedIn
#
# Every old URL that has ever been shared needs a line here. A 301 keeps the
# search equity and stops anyone who saved the link from hitting a 404.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── EXAMPLES — replace these with real old paths, do not ship as-is ──────────
# /home                     /            301
# /about-me                 /about/      301
# /services                 /advisory/   301
# /consulting               /advisory/   301
# /book                     /books/      301
# /from-africa-to-everywhere /books/     301
# /work-with-me             /contact/    301
# /booking                  /contact/    301
# /links                    /            301

# ── Old funnel or campaign paths, if any survive ─────────────────────────────
# /funnel/*                 /contact/    301
# /lp/*                     /            301

# ── Anything genuinely gone with no equivalent: let it 404 rather than
#    redirecting it to the homepage. A soft 404 to home is worse for search
#    than an honest 404, and it confuses the visitor.
